      "writtenOn": "2021-12-08T06:11:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suspect \"primary architecture\" may already be overloaded, but I see what you mean. I took out all the references for changing the \"primary\" out here, but am still reversing the order, as it\u0027s significantly less churn elsewhere to have Darwin[0] \u003d\u003d x86_64 / universal, since Darwin[1] can\u0027t execute on the host machine. And things should mostly work if mod[0] \u003d\u003d darwin[1] / mod[1] \u003d\u003d darwin[0].\n\nThat may get fuzzier when we support building on arm64, but it should still work. And there will be plenty of other changes required to get us there.",
      "parentUuid": "d4f940e1_f2a4acd5",
